## Why a fresh attempt is proposed

The approved first campaign terminated on its first investigator call with `transport_failure`; it evaluated no candidate and completed cleanup. The original exception was discarded, so its exact cause cannot be recovered from that journal. The key endpoint subsequently returned HTTP 200 and zero daily usage; the credits endpoint showed $25 purchased and $6.480485129 used. These account snapshots do not prove the first request was never received or settle its individual usage.

A reviewed local diagnostic now preserves allowlisted exception class, integer HTTP status, allowlisted error codes and up to eight local stack positions. It emits no exception message, body, headers or credentials and leaves ledger settlement unchanged. Static Ruff, compilation and independent source review passed. The evaluator source hash is unchanged; no image rebuild or baseline rerun is needed. **This is a diagnostic improvement, not a proven repair of the original transport failure.** The model request contract is unchanged. If a new request fails, stop and inspect its diagnostic; do not launch again automatically.

Approval here grants a fresh maximum of six calls and 448,000 tokens. Together with the original campaign's one conservatively accounted attempt and 18,497 reserved tokens, that is at most seven local role attempts and 466,497 accounted/reserved tokens across the two campaigns. Original recorded cost $0 is not verified per-request billing. The original terminal journal remains unchanged and is never resumed.

## What approval covers

- Model: `openai/gpt-5.4` through `https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/chat/completions`.
- OpenRouter selects a compatible upstream. No upstream provider is pinned and upstream failover is not explicitly disabled.
- At most **2 rounds, 6 role calls, 448,000 total tokens, and 8,192 output tokens per call**, including reasoning within the output accounting. One hypothesis and at most one candidate per round.
- **No automatic retries or schema repairs.** Uncertain accepted outcomes stop for reconciliation; no blind repeat call.
- **Cost is audited; there is no enforcing USD ceiling.** At the currently published $2.50/M input and $15/M output headline rates, using the total-token ceiling with all six maximum outputs gives about **$1.73**. This is arithmetic guidance, not a guaranteed price or spending cap; routed tiers, fees and actual usage can differ. [OpenRouter pricing](https://openrouter.ai/openai/gpt-5.4).
- Each role has up to 300 seconds; each round up to 2 hours; the campaign up to 4 hours. Local evaluation: quick 600 seconds, each discovery window 1,200 seconds, one evaluator at a time.
- Use the existing `OPENROUTER` entry in the main checkout `.env`, mapped only into the launch process's `OPENROUTER_API_KEY`. The key is used for API authentication, never inserted into model messages, logs or review artifacts.

